{
  "description": "AOS-714 / CAD-2710: shared valid and invalid cases for an enum view param's optional `labels`. Both readers wrap each `view` as the only entry of a screen's `views`, with navigation sections [customers, reports], and read it: Cadence cadence-core app_screen_decl validate_map, hosted apps/api readScreenViews. Keep this file byte-identical in both repos. Option-label text is refused when empty after removing Unicode White_Space characters and U+FEFF, or when it holds a control character, U+2028 or U+2029. AOS-732 (v2) adds view-level cases so the hosted reader accepts exactly what the Cadence checker accepts: a view label needs 1 to 8 locales but no `en`, an enum value may be blank, and `required: false`, `record_id: null` and `values: null` on a date or string param read as absent (see `projection`). Cases that need raw JSON (a repeated key) cannot be written here and are covered by the Cadence tests only.",
